I recently was re-watching an early season, and one of their immunity challenges was Dots, but with, like, ropes on, like, a beach.

00:36:05.160 --> 00:36:08.920
And I was like, you know what, I like Dots, and I like Survivor.

00:36:09.360 --> 00:36:15.480
I don't know if this is, like, if this, just because Dots is good doesn't make it, like, a great, exciting reality TV challenge.

00:36:16.140 --> 00:36:31.540
Dots, Sean, since you asked, is, uh, yeah, you've got a, you've got a paper full of a grid of Dots, and you, you, you and another player take turns drawing a line from either, either vertically or horizontally, no diagonals, from one dot to another.

00:36:31.540 --> 00:36:38.100
Yeah, yeah. You keep doing that until when, when one person closes a box, they own the box, and then they can go again.

00:36:38.460 --> 00:36:46.360
So it, if you, like, leave someone to be able to close a box, you can, like, cause a chain reaction, or now they can close, like, 20 in a row, or something like that.

00:36:46.420 --> 00:36:53.440
There is a, there is a great port of Dots on Nintendo Switch, uh, part of Clubhouse 51.

00:36:53.440 --> 00:36:57.200
I thought you were, I thought you were going to say a port of Dots on, like, the Magnet Doodle or something.

00:36:57.420 --> 00:37:08.700
Yeah. Uh, no, no, for real, Clubhouse 51, great, uh, game on the Switch, and it has many of these board games, and I think it has Othello as well, uh, might, might, they might be calling it Reversi.

00:37:08.860 --> 00:37:10.960
You know, there is a difference between Othello and Reversi.

00:37:11.020 --> 00:37:16.340
I always thought it was just, like, a, a language thing, or, like, a different, um, way of saying the same game.

00:37:16.360 --> 00:37:30.820
Like Hellman's Mayonnaise. Sure, um, but, uh, the difference is, is that Reversi has the fixed position, where, um, it's in the center, the four, the center four squares are black, white, black, white.

00:37:31.100 --> 00:37:34.320
Uh, so this way it's, uh, or sorry, black, white, white, black.

00:37:34.520 --> 00:37:41.520
So this way, um, it's a defined position, whereas in Othello, you can start in any position you want, um, which I think is interesting.

00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:46.060
One more thing I just wanted to talk about, which wasn't really, like, a flaw with the game, it's a flaw with me.

00:37:46.060 --> 00:37:53.660
But, like, was it ever unclear to anybody else which circles exactly were going to change for them?

00:37:53.880 --> 00:38:00.120
